<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Detailed overview of Established datasets</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional information regarding the test sets used for GenImage <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al. (2024)</a></cite>, ImagiNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boychev &amp; Cholakov (2024)</a></cite>, and Chameleon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al. (2025)</a></cite> in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Redefining Generalization in Visual Domains: A Two-Axis Framework for Fake Image Detection with FusionDetect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. It includes generators used, number of images, image resolution, semantic categories, and the source for real images utilized in these datasets which is shown in Tables <a href="#S7.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 7.2 Detailed overview of Established datasets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Redefining Generalization in Visual Domains: A Two-Axis Framework for Fake Image Detection with FusionDetect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <a href="#S7.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 7.2 Detailed overview of Established datasets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Redefining Generalization in Visual Domains: A Two-Axis Framework for Fake Image Detection with FusionDetect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, and <a href="#S7.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 7.2 Detailed overview of Established datasets ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Redefining Generalization in Visual Domains: A Two-Axis Framework for Fake Image Detection with FusionDetect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Note that the numbers reported in these tables indicate the count of fake images only.</p>
</div>
